---
title: Stuffing
image: https://thefoodcharlatan.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Traditional-Thanksgiving-Stuffing.jpg
---

> TL;DR: combine ingredients in the order of Moist -> Dry -> Wet.

Mix @apples{2}(Granny Smith, finely cubed), @raisins{2%cups}(about a 12oz box), @walnuts{2%cups}(chopped), @onion{1}(large, finely cubed), and @celery{}(enough to match the onion, cubed) in a #large bowl{}.

Add @bread crumbs or seasoned stuffing{1%bag} and @bread{.5%loaf}(fresh, cubed). Mix until combined.

In a separate #bowl, mix @milk{1.5%cups} and @butter{1.5%sticks}(melted).

> Use your best judgement with amounts here. Honestly you can use between 1.5 cups/sticks to 2. More butter is more buttery, more liquid is more liquidy. You probably know your preferences here.

Let the milk/butter mixture cool. Add @eggs{2} and mix well. Then, add back to your other bowl. Mix thoroughly.

Stuff your turkey with stuffing and cook (usually 350° F for 4 hours), and for the remaining stuffing, place in a pan and cook at 350°F for ~{30-45%minutes}